=== P3 Shared surface 0025 AiLimitBanner (Android) ===
# Gate note: the prompt addresses :app:, but this project's Gradle module path is :android:
#   (apps/android/settings.gradle.kts: "every P3/A* prompt gate addresses :android:"). Tasks corrected
#   :app: -> :android:; lint scoped to :android:. --no-daemon for isolation on a shared runner.
# Capability: Jetpack Compose + Material 3 present; project Kotlin 2.4.0 satisfies the prompt's ">= 2.2.x"
#   minimum -> NOT BLOCKED.
# Layout: surface shipped as the subdirectory shared-surfaces/AiLimitBanner/ (AiLimitBanner.kt +
#   AiLimitBannerModel.kt) so the gate's check-placeholders -Path and the commit's git add ...AiLimitBanner
#   address a real directory (matches the RouteAnnouncer / VisuallyHidden sibling surfaces). Pure-presentational
#   surface: composable + model only (no Source/ViewModel) — the web source's only hook is useTranslation, so
#   there is no data port to bind (mirrors the equally presentational RouteAnnouncer). Unit tests are pure-JVM
#   projection + diagnostics (the unit-test classpath has no Robolectric/Compose-test), so every per-state
#   branch is asserted through the pure classifier — the established pattern for these surfaces.
# i18n (Honesty Covenant #9 — disclosed, not silent): the ai.limit.* keys the web source uses (23) were absent
#   from the catalog. Added to the source of truth (web/src/i18n/en.json), the P1/S10 catalog
#   (apps/shared/i18n/catalog/en.json), and the Android default resource (values/strings.xml), matching
#   gen-i18n.ts output for these keys (retryIn -> "Try again in %1$ss"). A full gen-i18n regen was deliberately
#   NOT run: the committed resources already carry pre-existing drift (committed strings.xml has MORE keys than
#   the current source emits), so a blind regen would DELETE keys other committed surfaces depend on — out of
#   scope for this surface. ar/he/apple/windows are placeholder/other-platform artifacts not needed by this gate.
